  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Let, coordinate of any point on line is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is intersection point of plane &amp; line then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will lie on plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The distance of a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from origin&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>81</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi></math>units.</p>",
